course: dictionary
lesson: 9399
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word sprout can be a verb (something you do) or a noun (a thing). To find the right meaning, read the words around it. «A seed sprouts when it puts out its first shoot.» Here sprouts means starts to grow, because the seed is making a new plant.
explain: Now look at this sentence: «New shops sprouted up along the road.» Shops do not grow like plants, so sprouted must mean appeared suddenly. Always ask: does this meaning make sense in the sentence? If it does, you have found the right one.
explain: The word sprout can also be a thing. «Bean sprouts» are young shoots you can eat, and a «Brussels sprout» is a small green vegetable like a tiny cabbage. The words sprout up and bean sprouts help you know which meaning is needed.
fact: Sprout means to start to grow.
fact: A sprout is a young new shoot of a plant.
fact: A (Brussels) sprout is a small green vegetable like a tiny cabbage.
fact: To sprout can also mean to appear suddenly, as in «New shops sprouted up.»
fact: «Some lotus seeds found in a dry lake bed in China sprouted after about 1300 years.»
fact: «Green potatoes and potato sprouts contain a mild poison, so they should not be eaten.»
exercise: «A seed sprouts when it puts out its first shoot.» What does sprouts mean here? | Gets wet and dies | *Starts to grow | Turns into soil | Falls to the ground
exercise: «New shops sprouted up along the road.» What does sprouted up mean? | *Appeared suddenly | Fell down slowly | Were painted green | Were closed for the winter
exercise: Which word means a small green vegetable like a tiny cabbage? | Seed | *Brussels sprout | Root | Shoot
test: «Mangrove seeds sprout while still on the tree, then drop as long spikes.» What does sprout mean here? | Fall off the tree | Go dark and die | *Start to grow | Turn into wood
test: «Some lotus seeds sprouted after about 1300 years.» What does sprouted mean here? | *Began to grow after waiting a very long time | Were eaten by birds | Floated across the sea | Were found in a shop
exam: «Seeds that can wait help a plant survive bad years, sprouting when the drought or cold is over.» Why is it useful for a seed to wait? | It turns into a vegetable | *It can start growing again when conditions improve | It stops the seed from getting wet | Waiting makes the seed taste better
